loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:15: ## G1-1 â€” accept, fixed differently (severity: critical, plan.md:126, D10)
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:16: 
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:17: Claim: "D10 orders the draft-code gate to run even though the governing territory rule
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:18: requires a `loop/`-only diff to skip it."
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:19: 
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:20: The contradiction is real. The conductor contract (`.claude/agents/conductor.md:266-274`) and
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:21: the workflow (`.claude/skills/work/WORKFLOW.md:126-127`) both make the skip derived, not
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:22: judged. But the derived rule exists to block a self-granted LOOSENING â€” an orchestrator
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:23: exempting its own item from review. D10 goes the opposite direction: the derived answer is
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:24: skip, and the ruling orders the gate to RUN. A tightening may be proposed openly; that is
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:25: what D10 is.
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:26: 
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:27: The implied remedy â€” obey the derived skip â€” is rejected: skipping code review on a
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:28: ~400-line script rework is the wrong outcome. Disposition:
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:29: 
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:30: - D10 STANDS for this item. The conductor already carries the standing ruling in
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:31:   PHASE-STATE and has acknowledged it; gate 2 runs.
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:32: - The contract gap is FILED as standalone machinery work, in words, not built here: the
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:33:   derived skip needs one clarifying sentence in the conductor contract and the workflow â€”
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:34:   a derived SKIP is a floor an orchestrator ruling recorded in PHASE-STATE may tighten to
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:35:   RUN; a derived RUN may never be loosened to SKIP. This item's path-set does not include
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:36:   the process contracts, and the clarification stands alone.
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:37: 
loop/items/AI4DEV-80/gate1-rulings.md:38: ## G1-2 â€” accept, fixed differently (severity: critical, plan.md:137)
