84: ## 4. Decisions
85: 
86: - D1 **Usage is counted ONLY from `.jsonl` transcripts**: the top-level session files (as
87:   today) plus every `agent-*.jsonl` under each session's `subagents` tree â€” RECURSIVE,
88:   because 587 of the 877 real transcripts sit one level deeper, in
89:   `subagents/workflows/wf_<id>/` (draft ruling D-1; the flat glob this plan first wrote
90:   would have kept two thirds of the store invisible). Temp `.output` files leave the usage scan
91:   entirely. This lands ruled bullet 4 structurally (F5's file can never count again), avoids
92:   the twin double-count F4 proves, and loses nothing (zero orphan transcripts measured). The
93:   header's "transcript file(s)" count then counts scanned `.jsonl` transcripts only.
94: - D2 **The spawn forest comes from the meta files** (F2): role = `agentType` (the same
95:   spawn-call value the design names; the file-name pairing pass and its `.output` scan are
96:   deleted with D1), parent edge = `parentAgentId`, session root = the directory path (derived,
97:   never declared). A `.jsonl` with no meta (zero today) reads role `unmarked agent`, builds
98:   no edge, and is said in the output â€” never silent.
99: - D3 **Per-response resolution order** (existing rules first, one new fallback): own-record
100:   branch â†’ item (unchanged); stamp fallback for session files (unchanged); NEW for agent
101:   files: the agent's TREE-ITEM, labeled source `tree` in the From column. TREE-ITEM(agent) =
102:   first of: (a) the single distinct item the agent's own branch records resolve anywhere in
103:   its file (F3 makes this the common case; the whole-file discovery uses the SAME
104:   unescaped-only match shape as the existing per-record scan â€” an escaped `\"gitBranch\"`
105:   inside a tool result is never a branch fact, ruling G1-10); (b) ONLY when (a) finds ZERO
106:   items: TREE-ITEM(parent agent), walking `parentAgentId` upward with a visited-set cycle
107:   guard â€” no depth cap (ruling G1-5; the visited set must remain, as the removal
108:   condition); if (a) finds TWO OR MORE distinct items, the file's branchless responses stay
109:   unattributed and the floor note states the ambiguous-file count (ruling G1-4); (c) at a
110:   session root: the item the session had resolved (branch first, stamp fallback) at the
111:   spawn's `toolUseId` â€” the stamp is rendered from the chain cache `/work` maintains, which
112:   is exactly the ruled coordinator root (bullet 2). Unresolvable stays unattributed â€”
113:   degrade, never guess. A branch naming two items stays `unresolved` (unchanged).
114: - D4 **Tree-resolved responses feed the role table and `agentItem`** exactly as
115:   branch-resolved ones, so a sitting's tokens land under its item AND its role (ruled bullet
116:   3), and the kimi join keeps working. Join key note: subagents file base names carry an
117:   `agent-` prefix â€” strip it, keys stay bare agentIds.
118: - D5 **`-Days` filters which transcripts are usage-scanned** (unchanged semantics). Meta
119:   files are ALWAYS all read â€” 872 tiny files, and edges must exist even when a parent
120:   transcript sits outside the window. Spawn-context (D3c) is captured only from scanned
121:   sessions; a window that excludes the parent session loses that root, stated in the floor
122:   note. The default (`-Days 0`, all history) has no such gap.
123: - D6 **Testability seams**: the report gains root-override parameters â€” `-ProjectsDir`,
124:   `-AttrDir`, `-ItemsDir`, `-CodexSessions`, `-KimiRoot` â€” defaulting to today's hard-coded
125:   paths, plus a `-Json` switch that emits the aggregates (per-item rows, role rows, rollup
126:   rows, totals, unattributed %, AND the vendor aggregate tables `codexRows` and `kimiRows`
127:   â€” ruling G1-7) as one JSON object instead of tables. Default invocation output is
128:   unchanged. The selftest asserts on parsed JSON, not on `Format-Table` text â€” an exact
129:   oracle instead of a whitespace-brittle one.
